   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Your pod looks up one external API, and DNS sends extra queries first?"
  },
  {
   "id": "bug",
   "text": "Most devs never check this."
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "text": "Kubernetes sets n dots five. A name with fewer than five dots is tried with each cluster search domain before the real name."
  },
  {
   "id": "fix",
   "text": "Add a trailing dot to make the name fully qualified, or lower n dots in the pod's DNS config. Now the real name is tried first."
  },
  {
   "id": "bait",
   "text": "Trailing dot or DNS config? Comment which one you use."
  },
